    "risk_summary": "The A Eliashberg benefit is only 0.058 K (McMillan and Allen–Dynes +0.051 K), not a demonstrated robust improvement; the A fine F is 16.80 meV/atom higher. The support grade is for the bounded phase/network hypothesis with explicit opposite λ, not a significant global potential ranking.",
    "ambient_scope": "Exact model force/full stress, converged electronic outputs, reported finite-q workflow and raw Γ optical evidence provide a bounded near-ambient source-model screen. Source residual stress/metastable alternatives remain explicit; this is not proof of synthesizeability, full BZ or global equilibrium.",
    "route_response": "Both ordered tetragonal phases have strongly different Ru/Tc like-species separations (about 2.71258 versus 3.83478 Å). λ favors B in all ten rows, whereas ω and all three separate Tc products favor A. This is a geometry/pairing tradeoff vector, not monotonic λ optimization. Complete species-channel geometry differences and computed all-σ pairing response are saved against the frozen controls. Cell/grid/method sensitivity prevents a pure geometry-only causal claim; no bandwidth/carrier quantity is substituted.",
    "next_action": "Freeze A/B identity and test the tradeoff at matched grids and common product definitions. If all Tc benefits vanish or change sign while B keeps greater λ, downgrade the claim of A benefit; no maximum-σ or outcome-based comparator substitution.",
    "seven_criteria": {
      "identity": "Source-specific full-species CIF→both SCF inputs→Γ coordinate/cell association, actual atom order and origin, within 1e-6 Å observational matching policy. Original experimental occupancy and measured P/T unknown; configured QE neutral/nonmagnetic/no-SOC model is distinct from a magnetic ground-state claim.",
      "novelty": "One exact reduced composition/ordered phase-design group, new to the frozen reviewed cohort. Published computed source is acknowledged, known experimental chemistry remains a comparator. Bounded primary phase search has not tied the exact target order to an established SC sample; no global absence claim.",
      "quantitative_route_response": "Both ordered tetragonal phases have strongly different Ru/Tc like-species separations (about 2.71258 versus 3.83478 Å). λ favors B in all ten rows, whereas ω and all three separate Tc products favor A. This is a geometry/pairing tradeoff vector, not monotonic λ optimization. Complete species-channel geometry differences and computed all-σ pairing response are saved against the frozen controls. Cell/grid/method sensitivity prevents a pure geometry-only causal claim; no bandwidth/carrier quantity is substituted.",
      "pairing_relevance": "All ten source λ/ω rows retained with original units/nulls, and μ*=0.1 source McMillan, Allen–Dynes and Eliashberg products kept separate. Source Gaussian EPC broadening is distinct from explicit MP electronic SCF smearing. No product maximum or selected σ defines the recommendation.",
      "ambient_feasibility": "Exact model force/full stress, converged electronic outputs, reported finite-q workflow and raw Γ optical evidence provide a bounded near-ambient source-model screen. Source residual stress/metastable alternatives remain explicit; this is not proof of synthesizeability, full BZ or global equilibrium.",
      "competition_and_coherence": "The A Eliashberg benefit is only 0.058 K (McMillan and Allen–Dynes +0.051 K), not a demonstrated robust improvement; the A fine F is 16.80 meV/atom higher. The support grade is for the bounded phase/network hypothesis with explicit opposite λ, not a significant global potential ranking.",
